    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds like a good start. i'm also worried about the actual flow of the service. with 500 people, things get chaotic fast. do you have any advice on how to set up the buffet stations so the people with dietary restrictions don't get stuck in huge lines or accidentally grab the wrong thing because they're in a rush? maybe something about the layout or staff positioning?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To minimize congestion and ensure accessibility, consider organizing buffet stations with separate lines and stations for specific dietary requirements, such as nut-free and vegan options. Position staff near each station who can assist and communicate with guests about the options. Another idea is to designate ' escalating service lines' - where guests with severe allergies can be temporarily isolated in a quieter section, receiving assistance from a dedicated team. Having a mobile registration station where guests can declare their dietary requirements beforehand can also help streamline the process.",
      "source": "target",
